def get_slide_data() -> dict:
    return {
        'title': 'Execution 1 — Optimization Progress & Next Steps',
        'content': '\n## Execution 1: CCD Optimization Progress\n\n### Current CCD Sample Progress\n\nThe system is actively running 25 CCD samples overnight via `69_ThesisOptimization_bgTask.sh`.\nBased on the `StellarOrionIntentionLog.jsonl`, the **active sample** at last check was:\n\n```\nD = 3.356 m  |  θ = 60°  |  N = 6  |  Rn = 0.55 m  →  SPARTA Step 800 / 1100\n```\n\nThis corresponds to one of the **axial star points** in the CCD matrix (diameter axis probe).\n\n---\n\n### Baseline Optimization Flow Plots\n\nThese plots represent the **Phase 1 baseline** (IRVE-3 geometry) which the optimizer uses as the reference $F_{ref}$ for all 25 CCD comparisons:\n\n<div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:1rem 0;">\n  <div style="flex:1; min-width:280px;">\n    <img src="latestResult/opt_thermal_map_smooth_M0_A0.png"\n         style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(255,100,50,0.3);\n                box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />\n    <p style="color:#8b949e; font-size:0.72rem; text-align:center; margin-top:0.4rem;">\n      Baseline thermal map (IRVE-3, D=3.0m)\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div style="flex:1; min-width:280px;">\n    <img src="latestResult/opt_mach_map_smooth_M0_A0.png"\n         style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(76,201,240,0.3);\n                box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />\n    <p style="color:#8b949e; font-size:0.72rem; text-align:center; margin-top:0.4rem;">\n      Baseline Mach field — bow shock at baseline geometry\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<div style="display:flex; gap:1rem; flex-wrap:wrap; margin:1rem 0;">\n  <div style="flex:1; min-width:280px;">\n    <img src="latestResult/opt_upscaled_3d_grid_smooth_M0_A0.png"\n         style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(100,220,100,0.3);\n                box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />\n    <p style="color:#8b949e; font-size:0.72rem; text-align:center; margin-top:0.4rem;">\n      3D baseline temperature revolution\n    </p>\n  </div>\n  <div style="flex:1; min-width:280px;">\n    <img src="latestResult/opt_upscaled_3d_mach_smooth_M0_A0.png"\n         style="width:100%; border-radius:8px; border:1px solid rgba(200,160,255,0.3);\n                box-shadow:0 4px 16px rgba(0,0,0,0.5);" />\n    <p style="color:#8b949e; font-size:0.72rem; text-align:center; margin-top:0.4rem;">\n      3D Mach field — baseline shock structure\n    </p>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n---\n\n### Understanding the 1100-Step SPARTA Run\n\n**Q: Does 1100 steps = 11 ms of simulated time?**\n\nNo. Each step is $\\Delta t \\approx 0.6\\;\\mu$s, so:\n\n$$1100 \\times 0.6\\;\\mu\\text{s} = 0.66 \\text{ ms of simulated entry time}$$\n\nThis is intentional — DSMC does not simulate the full entry trajectory. It simulates a **snapshot** of the flow field at one instant during peak heating (Mach 9, ~60 km altitude). The 1100 steps are needed to average away the Monte Carlo noise and reach a **statistically stationary** flow field. Individual particles are stochastic; the averaged fluxes are deterministic to within CV < 10%.\n\n**Q: Is one SPARTA run enough per CCD sample?**\n\nYes — DSMC statistical noise is suppressed by averaging over all 11 dump snapshots (steps 100, 200, …, 1100). The CV = 7.3% for drag in the current run is within the acceptable MoP training tolerance.\n\n---\n\n### How Do We Conclude Validity When OpenFOAM Times Differ?\n\nAll 25 CCD samples use the **same** `endTime = 450 s` in the OpenFOAM `controlDict`, making them directly comparable. If a sample ever runs with a different duration (e.g. resumed after a crash), we normalise:\n\n- Extract $T_{backface}(t^*)$ from the time series at the canonical $t^* = 450$ s.\n- If $t < t^*$, re-run or extrapolate using the analytical 1D solution: $T(L,t) \\approx T_{surface} \\text{erfc}(L/2\\sqrt{D_T t})$.\n\nA run is **more physically valid** if:\n1. CV of SPARTA drag < 10% (converged flow statistics)\n2. OpenFOAM residuals < 1×10⁻⁶ (PCG converged)\n3. $T_{backface}$ is still **rising** at `endTime` — confirms transient regime captured, not capped at equilibrium.\n\n---\n\n### What to Do Next Week\n\n| Priority | Task | Why |\n|:---|:---|:---|\n| 🔴 **High** | Complete all 25 CCD samples | Need full design matrix to train MoP |\n| 🔴 **High** | Fix geometry watertight failures for remaining star-point geometries | Some edge cases (very small $D$, high $N$) still crash |\n| 🟡 **Medium** | Train MoP surrogate on completed CCD results | Can start with partial data (≥ 16 corners) |\n| 🟡 **Medium** | Run Genetic Algorithm on MoP | Requires MoP to be trained |\n| 🟡 **Medium** | Scale validated 3.0 m result up to 7.5 m (Orion) | Use analytical scaling laws for β and $\\dot{q}$ |\n| 🟢 **Low** | Add OpenFOAM time-series plots per sample | Visualise $T_{backface}(t)$ convergence |\n| 🟢 **Low** | Compare scalloped vs. smooth topology at optimum | Confirm "Scalloping Penalty" quantified |\n\n**Expected deliverable next week:** MoP surrogate trained on ≥ 16 CCD corner samples + first GA run showing optimised geometry candidates with $\\beta \\approx 148$–152 kg/m² and $T_{surface} < 1870$ K.\n'
    }
